config AUDIO_MT8188_AFE
	bool "MediaTek MT8188 Audio Front End"
	default y
	depends on DT_HAS_MEDIATEK_MT8188_AFE_ENABLED
	depends on CLOCK_CONTROL_MT8188_APMIXED
	depends on CLOCK_CONTROL_MT8188_TOPCKGEN
	depends on CLOCK_CONTROL_MT8188_INFRA_AO
	select PINCTRL
	help
	  Enable the Audio Front End, which moves samples between memory and
	  the die's eTDM serial ports.

	  The interface callers use is in
	  <zephyr/drivers/audio/mt8188_afe.h>.  It is not the Zephyr DAI
	  interface: the routing matrix, the channel-merge units and the
	  cowork'd port pairs have no expression in DAI.

	  The three clock controllers are required rather than selected because
	  the AFE reaches them through the clocks its devicetree node names, so
	  a configuration without them would not describe working hardware.
